Never let mobile feel cramped.
Cybersecurity buyers read on phones during travel.

---

# 4. Styling Techniques (Trending in 2026)

## Gradient Highlight Words

Use brand gradient on key words only.

Example:

Illuminate Every
**Threat Vector**

Where “Threat Vector” has a subtle blue → violet gradient.

Not entire sentences. Just emphasis.

---

## Section Divider Detail

Under H2, add:

• 2px subtle accent line
• 40–60px width
• Brand blue or violet

Minimal but intentional.

---

## Uppercase Usage

Avoid full uppercase headlines.

Use uppercase only for:

• Navigation items
• Small section labels
• Framework tags (ISO 27001, SOC 2)

And increase letter spacing for uppercase text:
0.08em to 0.12em

This adds sophistication.

---

# 5. CTA Typography

Primary Button:
Inter
16px
Weight: 500

Slight letter spacing 0.02em
No bold-heavy buttons. Modern UI uses medium weight.

---

# 6. Text Color Hierarchy (Dark Mode Optimized)

Primary Text → Soft white (#E6EDF3 type tone)
Secondary Text → Muted gray-blue
Inactive Text → 60% opacity

Never use pure white everywhere. It causes glare.

---

# 7. Hero Composition Example

H1 (Space Grotesk 64px)
Short 1–2 line statement.

Subtext (Inter 18px)
One clear value-driven sentence.

Primary CTA
Secondary CTA

Max 2–3 lines.
Whitespace around it.

Modern security websites breathe.

